  "body": "After #452 reached production, the real password-reset email reached Gmail INBOX with aligned SPF/DKIM/DMARC and its signed application Message-ID, but the successful SMTP events were absent from the recent Fly log stream. These two events used block-buffered stdout; the error event already used stderr. Send all three SMTP events through the same stderr stream so low-volume successful sends are observable immediately. No changes to delivery, content, authentication, configuration or recipient selection.\n\nValidation: Stack/GHC Email typecheck and six focused email tests passed (including 100 QuickCheck cases). A local pipe probe runs the actual Email module with a synthetic transport, pauses the process before exit and compares revisions: before, zero immediate events and two flushed at exit; after, both events immediately on stderr and zero deferred events. No network or real email was used in this probe. Hosted CI is in progress. Production follow-up will correlate one authorized Gmail test Message-ID with both smtp_attempt and smtp_accepted; no customer campaign is sent.\n",
